{
  "_readme": [
    "Registrable domain -> parent group id. Used only to collapse pages that",
    "share a corporate owner, so that two mastheads under one roof are counted",
    "as one newsroom rather than two independent confirmations.",
    "",
    "THIS MAP IS INCOMPLETE BY DESIGN, AND ITS INCOMPLETENESS IS A DOCUMENTED",
    "LIMITATION OF THE SYSTEM RATHER THAN A BUG. There is no public, complete,",
    "machine-readable register of world media ownership, and control changes",
    "faster than any seeded file can track. A domain that is absent here is",
    "treated as INDEPENDENT: the loader must never crash on an unknown domain,",
    "and must never guess a parent from a name or a substring.",
    "",
    "The direction of that error is deliberate. An absent domain makes",
    "independent_source_count too HIGH, which overstates corroboration, so a",
    "missing entry is visible as a claim looking better supported than it is.",
    "The opposite default -- guessing at shared ownership -- would silently",
    "erase real independent reporting, and a journalist would have no way to",
    "tell it had happened. Over-counting can be checked by hand; under-counting",
    "cannot.",
    "",
    "Group ids are coarse labels for grouping, not a corporate registry. They",
    "do not model minority stakes, joint ventures, licensing deals, or every",
    "change of control, and no ordering or quality judgement is implied by",
    "membership. Nothing here rates a publisher.",
    "",
    "Stored as JSON, not YAML, because PyYAML is not in backend/requirements.txt",
    "-- it happens to be in the current venv but nothing declares it, so a clean",
    "install would not have it. Data, loaded at runtime, never code."
  ],
